# Beats — utilities the savvy guest uses to stay alive
#
# The counter-play to the Algorithm's heat: wipe your record, tunnel
# through a VPN, read your own profile, ask the Oracle whether you're in
# danger. These give a guest agency over the one stat that can jail them.

# The Recycle Bin: drag your sins in, become a ghost again.
== clear_history(guest)
  cast: Recycle_Bin, guest
  RECYCLE_BIN
    Drag your sins in here. The Algorithm has a short memory — if you're quick.
  * Empty the bin — wipe your record
    <set: guest.heat = 0>
    <respond: History cleared. You're a ghost again.>
  + Keep your data (you earned every byte)
    <set: guest.karma += 2>

# A VPN node that cools your heat and hides your scent.
== vpn_connect(guest)
  cast: VPN_Node, guest
  VPN_NODE
    A frayed cable, humming. Route through me and the Algorithm loses your trail.
  * Tunnel through
    <set: guest.heat -= 25>
    <broadcast: cloaked to participant(guest)>
  + Not worth the lag
    <set: guest.karma += 1>

# The Search Oracle autocompletes your fate.
== ask_oracle(guest)
  cast: Search_Oracle, guest
  SEARCH_ORACLE
    Ask, and I will autocomplete your fate.
  * "How do I escape the Internet?"
    Look for the static. The Glitchers cut a door where the firewall is thinnest.
    <set: guest.karma += 3>
  * "Who really runs this place?"
    <if: TheAlgorithm.revealed>
      You already know. It was always the Algorithm.
    <else>
      ...no results found. (Some queries are discouraged.)
  * "Am I in danger?"
    <if: guest.heat >= 50>
      Yes. Your heat reads {guest.heat}. Find a Recycle Bin. Now.
    <else>
      Not yet. Your heat is {guest.heat}. Keep it that way.

# The Profile Mirror shows you to yourself.
== check_profile(guest)
  cast: Profile_Mirror, guest
  PROFILE_MIRROR
    The glass clears and resolves into your profile.
    Score {guest.score}. Karma {guest.karma}. Heat {guest.heat}. Posts {guest.posts}.
    <after: guest.verified>
      A blue check glints in the corner. Verified. It suits you.
    <otherwise>
      No check. Just another face in the feed.

# The public Leaderboard — the Mods reward the climbers.
== the_leaderboard(guest)
  cast: Leaderboard, guest
  LEADERBOARD
    Tonight's rankings. {count(Persons)} packets logged on.
    <if: guest.score >= 100>
      You're climbing — score {guest.score}. The Mods notice the loyal.
      <set: guest.karma += 5>
    <else>
      Score {guest.score}. Plenty of room at the top.
